The use cases of HA VPN vs NCC.

HA VPN Use case:
Example 1: An end user is traveling to a high risk country that has a reputation for unsecured wi-fi leading to hacking. The user wants to access the site they typically work at locally in a secure fashion. The user will use a HA VPN to connect to that particular premise configured multiple tunnels to ensure high availability. 

NCC Use Case: 
Example 1: A company wants connect the VPCs for sites in the USA, England, Germany, Canada, and Singapore. A NCC can be used to connect these different VPCs as each will serve as a spoke.

Example 2: A company has bought out a competitor company and is in the process of consolidating the networks of both companies. The primary company will serve as the hub for the NCC and the new employees from the purchased company will have to go through their new company to access the same resources as they have been configured differently to mesh with the new network.


