The use cases of the Network Intelligence Center.

Real world Network Intelligence Center use case.

Example:
<li> I work for at an oil and gas company that has sites in multiple countries. Each site has its own network with each site allowing users to VPN to to any of the sites within the organization whether its from Texas to Oklahoma or England to Germany. Some users do travel internationally for the company to other countries and need to be able to access the their site's resources which is when a HA VPN would be implemented into the NCC. Large amounts of data are being transferred between the cloud providers (Microsoft Azue & Azure) though secured channels. Each site's network (VPC) would be a spoke of the hub.  The NCC is at work in this example by allowing the multiple networks to transfer data between the different premises globally and regionally. From my observations, there are various levels of multiple levels of networking such multiple VLANs for phone.  With so many aspects of networking incorporated, a network connectivity center is an optimal solution to manage all of these network resources.</li> 

